{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /workspace/tools.py read unirank-benchmark-v2 --find Zenith --lines 15'","aggregated_output":"/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n/bin/bash: warning: setlocale: LC_ALL: cannot change locale (C.UTF-8)\n{\n  \"id\": \"unirank-benchmark-v2\",\n  \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.19987v2\",\n  \"version\": \"arxiv:2607.19987v2\",\n  \"access_scope\": \"Cached section2.3 method descriptions; not an original-method full-paper audit.\",\n  \"text_sha256\": \"34ff9c412b35f3118aae377faca5f658d7bffac0b4ef1c12a4eb0c7937372789\",\n  \"total_lines\": 39,\n  \"start_line\": 11,\n  \"next_line\": 26,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"text\": \"11: RankMixer (Zhu et al., 2025) pools the history with target attention, tokenizes concatenated ranking fields into chunks, and alternates parameter-free Token Mixing with per-token MLPs.\\n12: •\\n13: Zenith (Zhang et al., 2026) separately embeds user and item identifiers, pools historical item attributes with target attention, tokenizes context and target attributes, and applies Zenith interaction blocks.\\n14: •\\n15: TokenMixer (Jiang et al., 2026) combines target-aware sequence summaries with global and group tokens, then applies reversible token mixing and per-token feed-forward networks.\\n16: •\\n17: UniMixer (Ha et al., 2026) flattens histories with user and context fields, then chunk-tokenizes them for UniMixing-Lite blocks.\\n18: •\\n19: HeMix (Wang et al., 2026) combines fixed and feature-conditioned queries with low-rank token mixing over recent and earlier histories.\\n20: •\\n21: SSR (Yu et al., 2026) uses target-attention sequence pooling and multi-view competitive sparse filters with dense fusion.\\n22: 2.3.2. Layer-wise Unified Interaction\\n23: This paradigm integrates sequential and non-sequential representations throughout every network layer.\\n24: •\\n25: OneTrans (Zhang et al., 2025) injects sequence and partitioned non-sequential tokens into every block, using mixed attention, a shared sequence FFN, and token-specific FFNs.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
