{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast,hashlib,json,subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrun=json.loads(subprocess.check_output(['python3','/workspace/tools.py','resolve','run://r-001']))\nprotocol=run['required_study_protocol_ref']; remain=run['context']['remaining_seconds']\nconfigs={}\nfor f in ['candidate.py','attribute15.py','uniform15_control.py','full16_control.py']:\n tree=ast.parse(Path(f).read_text())\n configs[f]=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\nsha={f:hashlib.sha256(Path(f).read_bytes()).hexdigest() for f in configs}\nrefs=['baseline-din','g2-r0004-context_only','g1-r0006-embedding_half','g1-r0006-dense_half','g1-r0007-table8_interact16','g1-r0010-copy16_interact16','g1-r0011-context8_item16','g1-r0013-id8_attr16','g1-r0013-id16_attr8','g1-r0015-coupled_item8_action16','g1-r0016-coupled_item12_action16','g1-r0016-coupled_item14_action16','g1-r0017-native_item14_action16_control','g1-r0017-native_item15_action16_control','g1-r0019-interior14','g1-r0019-full16_replay','g1-r0019-drop15_replay','g1-r0019-drop0_replay']\nassert set(refs)<=set(run['context']['allowed_observation_ids'])\nheld=['protocol '+protocol+'; released data identity 9f110bfc2f037f36e2f48787b812df640fe5df2de1cda8db7ac04590c1c9be44 and official_offline history','all permitted fields/labels/masks, 100-event history, 10 blocks and 30 uniform/feedback slots, count weighting and unnormalized scorer','context16/action16, scorer64/32, four towers128/64, Dice, source gradient gates (auxiliary scorer/item blocked; context allowed)','exact retained full16 scratch-initialized table/scorer/tower coordinates and unchanged other tensors; same ending CPU RNG/device RNG and host example order, subject to numerical gates','frozen seed20262027, one pass, batch8192, loss, split optimizers, learning rates, precision and full validation scoring']\nconfounds=['Single frozen seed; dimension deletion changes the learning trajectory and cannot establish intrinsic redundancy of a learned coordinate or robust retention. Existing deterministic replays are not repetitions.','Different groups save different parameter counts and arithmetic widths; ID15/attribute16 and ID16/attribute15 are not capacity-matched and cannot rank semantic value per parameter. This is a factorial intervention, not a pure representation-only effect.','Hardware shape effects, host load and loader overhead may dominate inference savings; no FLOP-derived speedup claim. The scratch full16 construction costs CPU time/memory and must be included.','Repeated validation-guided search makes these exploratory comparisons. Source initialization and protocol transfer across seeds remain untested; diagnostics status not_requested is not a numerical parity certificate.']\ncontrasts=[]\nfor intervention,control in [\n ('id15_attr16 minus full16_replay: delete coordinate15 only from advertisement item_id, including corresponding scorer/tower columns.','full16_replay; existing g1-r0019-full16_replay and g2-r0004-context_only are exact-parity historical anchors.'),\n ('id16_attr15 minus full16_replay: delete coordinate15 only from all other supplied source=item fields.','full16_replay; existing g1-r0019-full16_replay.'),\n ('uniform15_replay minus id15_attr16, and uniform15_replay minus id16_attr15: conditional deletion contrasts; interaction I=A(15,15)-A(15,16)-A(16,15)+A(16,16).','The four concurrent cells form a 2x2 deletion factorial. uniform15_replay must reproduce g1-r0019-drop15_replay; full16_replay must reproduce source. Existing severe native-width g1-r0013-id8_attr16 and g1-r0013-id16_attr8 remain contextual evidence, not matched controls.')]:\n contrasts.append({'parent_ref':'g1-r0019-drop15_replay','intervention':intervention,'control':control,'held_fixed':held,'remaining_confounds':confounds,'decision_if_supported':'Keep any lower-cost nondominated candidate on the exploratory click-AUC/cost frontier. If a mixed cell has better AUC than uniform15 and near-source quality, reserve later authorized paired seeds and closest controls before a robustness claim. Interpret factorial signs only at this fixed seed.','decision_if_not_supported':'Keep the unchanged source as quality incumbent and retain uniform15 as an explicitly lossy cost tradeoff; stop this field-group attribution branch unless a new discriminating observation justifies it. Do not expand coordinate search or reinterpret failure as proof against compression.'})\nquality='Primary selection and factorial contrasts use full validation click AUC, not four-task mean. Report continuous paired deltas to full16, uniform15 and baseline-din, all four task AUC/Logloss, auxiliary mean separately, and sample/positive/negative counts. As a prospective exploratory screen, absolute source click-AUC loss <=0.0002 with fewer persistent parameters and lower measured model p50/p95 latency is considered a near-retention lead; this tolerance is a research choice informed by prior data, not a statistical noninferiority margin or user deployment requirement. Exact equality/negative deltas remain visible. No significance claim without independent seeds and permitted clustered uncertainty.'\ngates='Host gates before scientific interpretation: full16 must match unchanged g2-r0004-context_only initial parameters/buffers/predictions and ending CPU RNG at identical incoming state; uniform15 must match g1-r0019-drop15_replay state and operator. Device RNG and host example order must remain identical. For each mixed cell audit exact prefix table copies by field; semantic query/key/difference/product/action and target/pooled column copies; unchanged context/action/hidden/bias/Dice buffers; local FeatureMap nonmutation, actual table alias identity, padding, registered persistent parameter counts and absence of registered scratch state. Require finite four-task forward/default BCE/backward, empty/padded/masked-history tests, target-action invariance, correct auxiliary gradient blocks and allowed context gradient, primary-only persistent scorer Dice updates. A failed gate is an implementation failure, not scientific counterevidence; preserve costs and correct before dependent interpretation.'\nmeasurement='Measure persistent/trainable total/embedding/dense counts, construction CPU time and peak memory, allocated GPU seconds, train wall/time/examples and peak GPU bytes, model-only whole-batch p50/p95 and throughput at8192, and loader-inclusive inference wall. History bins empty/1-16/17-64/>64 already exist and remain exploratory, with N/positive/negative counts; report insufficient slices. Hour/composition/frequency/missing-field slices and paired user-cluster bootstrap require an authorized host interface supplying the necessary metadata/predictions; none is exposed here. Do not invent timestamps, raw IDs, frequencies or independent-sample confidence intervals. No raw data/checkpoints/GPU/tensor runtime or scoring interface is available locally. The host readiness/data/visibility receipts and frozen protocol are inherited, not reverified by this coding phase.'\nstudy={\n'id':'g1-r0020-source-coupled-id-attribute-deletion-factorial',\n'protocol_ref':protocol,\n'evidence_refs':refs,\n'question':'Can source-aligned coordinate15 deletion in only the advertisement-ID group or only item-attribute fields preserve source click quality at lower measured cost, and which group or interaction accounts for the uniform15 tradeoff?',\n'hypothesis':'Observation: source g2-r0004-context_only AUC0.660646940486458 uses32060453 parameters and measured model p50=11.726ms. The latest full16 replay matches that AUC (p50=11.761ms); uniform prefix15 g1-r0019-drop15_replay gives0.6605886110435017 (loss0.0000583294429563),30536464 parameters and p50=9.581ms. Removing coordinate0 instead gives0.6601641008760506; removing both endpoints gives0.6601860848903449, so effects are not monotone in width or position. Mechanism hypothesis: coordinate15 deletion across all item fields mixes advertisement-ID and attribute contributions; its small net effect may conceal a useful coordinate in one group offset by removal elsewhere. A mixed-width native model with common full16 scratch initialization can isolate those contributions while retaining actual sparse/dense savings. Previous severe native reductions favored ID16/attribute8 (0.6596593) over ID8/attribute16 (0.6582329), but they confound initialization and cannot dictate the new result. '+quality,\n'nearest_work':[\n {'source_ref':'trial://g1-r0019-drop15_replay; /workspace/history_g1_r0019_drop15_replay.py sha256=58bdbab19b4d1917ec058e65f51fa0f230cb689706ad31d01c5bd2166cada8f2','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Closest implementation: generalized the source-coupled native-width constructor and semantic first-layer column mapping from uniform item15 to independent item_id15/16 and remaining item-attribute15/16 factors; no change in forward operators.'},\n {'source_ref':'paper:din content-sha256:5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2, primary text lines56-130 and258-302','verification':'read','difference':'Inherit adapted target-conditioned unnormalized local activation and Dice; retain existing UF compression/four-task path gates. This is capacity attribution in a prior adaptation, not an exact original DIN reproduction or new attention mechanism.'},\n {'source_ref':'unirank-code:Zenith git:90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d, sha256=baec072d207e4bdeae270ec6950fc086ea68ea98fbb6502b5c8d5d848ad74f58, lines59-101 and131-160; unirank-method-zenith','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Pinned benchmark source separately allocates ID embeddings and other fields. We adopt only the group-specific capacity contrast already motivated by local evidence. We do not adopt expanded ID tokens, tokenizer or interaction blocks, and never supply unavailable user IDs. Original paper:zenith full text is unavailable in the authorized registry; fallback unirank-benchmark-v2 lines11-25 was read. No original-paper reproduction or priority claim; novelty remains unverified.'},\n {'source_ref':'framework:unirank/pytorch/layers/embeddings/feature_embedding.py lines40-174 and framework:unirank/pytorch/models/rank_model.py lines307-371; pinned upstream90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Mirror native ordered shared-table ownership, per-field embedding_dim and reset order without editing host metadata, inputs, recipes or scores.'}],\n'inherited_components':['All forward methods of _NativeModel from history_g1_r0019_drop15_replay.py remain AST-identical: representation, UF compression, interactions, auxiliary functional scorer with cloned Dice buffers, count pooling and four-task forward.','Source full16 scratch construction, fork_rng(devices=[]) native construction and source-state copying: preserves full16 ending CPU stream; no trained checkpoint or teacher.','Frozen data, labels, metadata ownership and host protocol; context16/action16 and source auxiliary gradient gates; four separate towers and default sum of four unweighted BCEs.'],\n'proposed_difference':'A 2x2 ID-width(15/16) by item-attribute-width(15/16) deletion factorial. Only public field name item_id defines the advertisement-ID group; all other supplied source=item nonmeta fields are attributes. Each group retains prefix coordinates0..width-1. Generalize local alias-aware metadata layout and field-specific source-column/table copying. Expose four standalone modules with literal CONFIG: candidate.py=id15_attr16, attribute15.py=id16_attr15, uniform15_control.py=uniform15_replay, full16_control.py=full16_replay. Predicted persistent total/embedding/dense counts, derived from prior group contrasts and uniform15 receipts: id15_attr16=31212361/30946404/265957; id16_attr15=31384556/31123719/260837; uniform15=30536464/30276907/259557; full16=32060453/31793216/267237. Host must verify actual aliases/counts; these are predictions, not new measurements. '+gates+' '+measurement,\n'predictions':['At least one mixed cell should retain source click AUC more closely than the uniform15 cell if group-specific cancellation explains its net effect; no sign or significance is assumed. Provisional ID16/attribute15 preference from severe-width history is weak and explicitly initialization-confounded.','Both mixed cells have fewer parameters than full16 and more than uniform15; native interaction widths decrease without expansion maps. Measured inference savings may be smaller or absent due to kernel shape effects.','Full16 and uniform15 concurrent controls reproduce prior fixed-seed AUCs within host numerical reproducibility; this validates implementation consistency, not generalization or repetition.','The factorial interaction is reported whether positive, null or negative; it concerns this fixed-seed training intervention and does not establish semantic-group importance at equal capacity.'],\n'falsifiers':['Failed state/RNG/operator/masking or gradient gates invalidate the comparison; a successful training status alone is insufficient evidence of parity.','Neither mixed cell improves the source-relative quality/cost frontier, or either has no measured inference saving despite reduced parameter count: the proposed practical allocation benefit is unsupported in this range.','Mixed deletions yield additive similar losses with negligible interaction: the cancellation/interaction explanation is unsupported even if a smaller model remains a useful tradeoff.','Later authorized paired seeds show loss beyond the research screen or reverse group ordering: robust retention/group conclusions fail. They cannot be replaced by repeated identical-seed replays.'],\n'alternative_explanations':['Review of trajectories: naive embedding/dense halving